    "q-133371": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133371",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ evaluate ${f}_{xyx}(1,\\pi )$ if ${f}_{xx}(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$",
      "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyx}(x,y) & ={f}_{xxy}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{e}^{xy}\\cdot (-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{e}^{xy}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,1):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{xyx}(1,\\pi )={1}^{3}{e}^{1\\cdot \\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi ))=-{e}^{\\pi }\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
