    "q-133373": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133373",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ evaluate ${f}_{yxy}(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ if ${f}_{xy}(x,y)=7+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$",
      "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxy}(x,y) & ={f}_{xyy}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{yxy}(6,\\frac{\\pi }{3})=6\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=3\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
